 *
 * GENERATED from core/src/builtin_transports.cpp.in — DO NOT EDIT the generated copy.
 *
 * Each call below carries a `// builtin: <kind>` marker. A generator keeps the call of
 * every transport its build compiles, drops the marker, and deletes the line of every
 * other kind, so a dropped transport contributes neither its glue TU nor a call here and
 * nothing references it. Module selection is by which TUs get compiled, with no
 * preprocessor macros. The two generators, which tools/check_builtin_transports.py holds
 * byte-identical on every kind set:
 *   - `libtracer_generate_builtin_transports` in core/cmake/libtracer_sources.cmake, at
 *     configure time, for core/CMakeLists.txt and the ESP-IDF component;
 *   - integrations/platformio/libtracer_builtin_transports.py, from the PlatformIO build
 *     script, which has no CMake.
 * Self-registration was rejected: a static initialiser in an archive member nothing
 * references does not survive static linking.
